    <region left="234" top="14805" width="548" height="128" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Note: Maximum tension found at the top face of the plank is+ 5.00 N/mm2 . This is within<br />the class 3 hypothetical tensile stress of 5.5N/mm2 (0.2 mm crack width) for C40 concrete.<br />The top section will eventually be under permanent compression as the interface is above<br />the neutral axis of the composite action. Another point to note is that the construction live<br />load is transient and when it is removed, the actual tension at the top face over the<br />propping support is (3.57 + 0.23) = 3.8 N/mm2 , which is well within class 3 stresses with<br />0.1 mm crack width. Cracks at the top face over the prop, if any, will not affect the<br />structural integrity of the planks.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
